{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":502181,"name":"Ahmed Elkiki","username":"Ahmed_Elkiki","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/a587f6/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-27T17:33:29.247Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502181-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502181-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502181-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502181-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince updating Grok Bot about a week ago (around September 20, 2026), none of my bots can be loaded. The app shows “Can’t reach your computer. Your Bots are safe, they just can’t be loaded right now.” Retry does nothing. Recover computer fails. Reset fails with “The reset couldn’t finish. Grok Bot’s computer may be in a partial state.” In-app Send Feedback also fails with “We couldn’t deliver this report.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502181-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502181-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen Grok Bot.\u003cbr\u003e\nSidebar shows “Can’t reach your computer.”\u003cbr\u003e\nClick Retry: no change.\u003cbr\u003e\nClick Recover computer: fails.\u003cbr\u003e\nRun Reset: fails, partial state warning.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502181-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502181-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAgent computer reachable, bots load, files and logins preserved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502181-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502181-scr